## Diff In Docker Save and Docker Export 
 
  
# Save 

Target   - container to Images
output   - Full Image ( Layers, History, Metadata )
Best for - Moving images between hosts/registries

Note = Layer Preservation: It keeps every single layer and the history of the image intact.
       Metadata Retention: All original configurations (ports, volumes, entry points) are preserved.


# Import

Target   - Container to Tar
Output   - A single flat filesystem (no history)
Best For - Creating a "snapshot" of a container's current state

Note = Docker takes the current state of a container's filesystem and zips it up.
       Data Loss: You lose the metadata defined in the original Dockerfile, such as ENV variables, EXPOSE ports, and the ENTRYPOINT/CMD



