############### ->   NETWORK

Notes -- Docker Bridge -> when install docker , docker create a virtual bridge on your hostmachine #docker0
 
      -- IP Assignment: Docker’s internal DHCP service assigns a private IP address (usually in the 172.17.x.x range) to the container’s eth0 interface.

      -- Port mapping : -p 8080:80 -> Docker creates an iptables DNAT rule // traffic hitting the host 8080 is automatically redirected to container's private IP at port 80

     

! Docker Network Flow                                 # virtual ethernet - when you run or start container a veth is create for connection 

  eth0     -----        docker0              -----      veth(any number)        -----     container's eth0       
 
Host Nic        virtual Bridge on you VM               connect to container's            use to connect veth
                     ( 172.17.0.1 )                           eth0


